# Jonlib - zlib license, Copyright (c) 2026 Jonathan Peris.
# Image/color algorithms adapted from raylib 6.0 rtextures.c; shared math in Jonmath.
# Collision queries adapted from the same release's rshapes.c; file and path
# utilities from rcore.c.
# 3D collision queries adapted from rmodels.c; cameras from rcamera.h and rcore.c;
# text and codepoint utilities from rtext.c; WaveFormat's conversion from the
# miniaudio vendored by raudio.c (src/convert.bend, LICENSES/miniaudio.txt);
# the headless frame, shape and texture drawing from rcore.c, rlgl.h, rshapes.c,
# rtextures.c and rlsw.h (MIT, LICENSES/rlsw.txt); input, automation events,
# frame timing and gestures from rcore.c, rcore_memory.c and rgestures.h;
# fonts, text measurement and drawing from rtext.c and rtextures.c.
# Altered Bend implementations; see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and LICENSES/raylib.txt.
#
# Sections, in order (each starts with a "# ----" banner):
#   1. Data utilities: compression, Base64, checksums and splines
#   2. Geometry and collision
#   3. Cameras: rcamera.h and the rcore.c camera/screen-space queries
#   4. Colors
#   5. Random streams and owned-buffer storage
#   6. Image types and errors
#   7. Raw pixel bytes (GetPixelDataSize, GetPixelColor, SetPixelColor)
#   8. RGBA8 kernels: generation, color, drawing, geometry and resampling
#   9. Shared file boundary: suffix rules, bounded reads and closed writes
#   10. Surface: the public image API, dispatching on pixel format
#   11. Codecs, exporters, writers and loaders
#   12. Files: rcore.c path and file-data utilities
#   13. Logging and memory: TraceLog, MemAlloc/MemRealloc/MemFree
#   14. Audio waves: raudio.c Wave loading, editing and export
#   15. Text: rtext.c byte strings and UTF-8 codepoints
#   16. Input, gestures and timing: rcore.c CORE.Input and timing, rgestures.h
#   17. Frame and shapes: rcore.c frame, rlgl.h/rlsw.h rendering, rshapes.c, rtextures.c
#   18. Fonts and text drawing: rtext.c fonts, measurement and DrawText*, ImageText*
#   19. Header enumerations (generated by tools/enums_probe.py --write)
# Functions must be defined before use, so kernels precede the Surface layer
# that dispatches to them.
